{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3957","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3957","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3957\",\"parent_revision\":\"8d04b22448b83d45d8b77535d96206eeab85759f04c4019104a509a2f97f6ffe\",\"root_revision\":\"8d04b22448b83d45d8b77535d96206eeab85759f04c4019104a509a2f97f6ffe\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-26\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nIn live e2e run 36243404890 (main at 2e12e4ca8), the MCP backend status line read `\\\"Backend items (2 open / 1 total)\\\"`. An open count cannot exceed the total, so at least one of the two counts is wrong. The line comes from `_probe_backend_status` in `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/`.\\n\\nObserved only in the run's phase journal. Nobody has investigated it. It was not in scope for #3956, which fixed empty `backlog_list` results.\\n\\nImpact: an agent reads this line to judge backlog health, and a count that contradicts itself either misleads that judgement or teaches the agent to ignore the line.\\n\\nReproduction starting point: download the artifacts of run 36243404890 (`gh run download 36243404890 --repo Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills`) and find the line in the per-phase JSONL journal. The two counts may come from different sources, for example the live snapshot and the writer cache. If so, the mismatch may relate to the #3868 live-first change or the #3956 priority/section defect, where items without a section were dropped from one view but not the other.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Live e2e run 36243404890 journal, found while diagnosing PR #3956\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-26\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"6df173023bf11497385569825671d2b9b8f12aea23822ec00eaa25d246a4f75f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXNuMzw\"}"}